# component: radio-group
# decisions: A11Y-2, DOC-1, DOC-2, FOC-1, FOC-12, FOC-5, FOC-6
# hunks:
#   FOC-1, FOC-6: `outline-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-3
#     focus-visible:ring-ring/50` and the `aria-invalid` halo rings are removed.
#   FOC-5: the invalid tint and its checked counterpart become
#     `not-focus:aria-invalid:border-destructive` and
#     `not-focus:aria-invalid:aria-checked:border-primary`, so focus outranks the error colour.
#   FOC-12: the two `group-has-[:focus-visible]/field-label:` rules are removed with the choice
#     card's ring they existed to cancel — this system rings the control, not the card.
#   A11Y-2: the group's row rhythm goes from `gap-2` to `gap-3`. Each item carries a 32px-tall
#     invisible hit area (`after:-inset-y-2` on a 16px control), and an 8px gap puts adjacent rows
#     28px apart centre to centre — so the areas OVERLAP by 4px and the later sibling wins the
#     shared band, which `test/geometry.browser.test.tsx` measures with a real `elementFromPoint`
#     probe. 12px puts the centres exactly 32px apart: the areas touch and every target is
#     unobstructed. This is the A11Y-2 audit the exception map asks for on `radio-group`.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file, and `registry-stamp.mjs` writes the provenance header the
#               three-copy model needs (DOC-1); those hunks carry no decision of their own.
